1
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,290
说一件关于我们婚礼的事情
Some news of our wedding,

2
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:08,070
我给各位发了一封"空出时间"电邮
I have sent you all a "Save the date" e-mail.

3
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,870
太好啦  你们选好日子了吗
Oh, exciting. You guys picked a date?

4
00:00:09,870 --> 00:00:12,580
何止如此  我选好了80个日子
Better. I picked 80 dates.

5
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,740
我需要你们空出全部日子  直到名单缩小
And I need you to save them all until we narrow it down.

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:18,230
我还以为我们同意选6月15了
I thought we agreed on June 15.

7
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:20,220
那是美国国旗日隔天
That's the day after Flag Day.

8
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:22,730
大家肯定庆祝到虚脱了
Everyone'll be partied out.

9
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:25,000
选个日子而已  干脆点
It's a date-- just pick one.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,420
这不止是一个日子  这是经典的最佳化问题
It's not just a date-- it's a textbook optimization problem.

11
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:30,140
绝对有个最佳日期  就像是有
There is a perfect date-- just like there's

12
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,760
最佳室温与最佳餐后甜品一样
a perfect room temperature and a perfect dessert.

13
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,510
才没有最佳餐后甜品呢
Mm. There's no perfect dessert.

14
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:36,160
恐龙形状的海绵蛋糕
Yellow cake in the shape of a dinosaur

15
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:37,050
撒上巧克力糖霜
with chocolate frosting,

16
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:38,650
边上配一勺香草冰淇淋球
a scoop of vanilla ice cream on the side,

17
00:00:38,650 --> 00:00:40,450
不碰到蛋糕
not touching.

18
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:41,470
到时候你就知道了
You'll see.

19
00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:43,960
你会在我们婚礼上吃到
You'll have it at our wedding.

20
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,380
来打赌吗
You wanna bet?

21
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:47,960
你们给我足够时间
You give me enough time,

22
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,930
我也能够为婚礼算出完美日子
I can do the same thing with a wedding date--

23
00:00:49,930 --> 00:00:51,400
它必须是在周末
it needs to be on the weekend,

24
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,020
避开你们任何人的生日
uh, not near any of your birthdays,

25
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:54,650
或漫展周末
or the weekend of Comic Con.

26
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:56,300
你也可以在漫展上结婚啊
Ooh, you could get married at Comic Con.

27
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:58,550
-不行  -不行
- No! - No!

28
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,170
我们只需要选一个
We just need a weekend date

29
00:01:00,170 --> 00:01:02,470
无聊又平凡的普通周末就行了
that's completely boring and uneventful.

30
00:01:02,470 --> 00:01:04,020
让你们不把事情都安排好
Too bad you didn't get your ducks in a row,

31
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,170
不然其实今晚完美符合你条件呢
'cause tonight would have been perfect.

32
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
生

33
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
活

34
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
大

35
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
爆

36
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
炸

37
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,810
第十一季  第三集

38
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:39,650
早安
Good morning.

39
00:01:39,650 --> 00:01:41,170
早安啊
Good morning.

40
00:01:41,170 --> 00:01:44,580
我知道今天是吃苹果脆片的日子  但没有了
I know today is Apple Jacks day, but... we're all out.

41
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:47,810
没事  我吃什么都行
That's fine. I'll have anything.

42
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:48,820
真的假的
Really?

43
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,090
是啊  你懂的
Yeah. You know...

44
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:53,470
无所...
whatev.

45
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:55,630
"无所[谓]"吗
"Whatev"?

46
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:57,490
我喜欢你的这面
I like this side of you.

47
00:01:57,490 --> 00:01:59,360
那你知道我喜欢什么吗
You know what I like?

48
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:02,010
柔和爵士
Smooth jazz.

49
00:02:03,020 --> 00:02:06,020
Feels so good - Chuck Mangione

50
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:25,630
提醒你一下
Hey, just a reminder--

51
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:27,990
-今天下班后我要去喝酒  -很好
- I'm going out for drinks after work. - Oh. Great.

52
00:02:27,990 --> 00:02:31,400
提醒你一下  你有孕在身
Just a reminder-- you're pregnant.

53
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:34,680
我自己不喝  只是带新同事去
I'm not drinking, just taking a new coworker out.

54
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:38,120
提醒你一下  你是有夫之妇
Oh. Just a reminder-- you're married.

55
00:02:38,470 --> 00:02:40,150
女同事
Female coworker.

56
00:02:40,150 --> 00:02:42,640
初来乍到  我想让她感觉有家的温暖
She's new in town, and I want to make her feel welcome.

57
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,550
以及在大家跟她说我很毒辣之前
And let her know the office is full of liars

58
00:02:44,550 --> 00:02:47,900
先灌输她办公室都是说谎精的思想
before everyone tells her I'm mean.

59
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,250
她单身吗
Is she single?

60
00:02:49,250 --> 00:02:51,600
我才不要撮合她跟拉杰
I'm not setting her up with Raj.

61
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,410
-那斯图尔特呢  -你是没听我说话吗
- What about Stuart? - Are you listening?

62
00:02:53,410 --> 00:02:56,610
我想要她觉得我是暖心好人
I want her to think I'm not mean.

63
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:57,950
好吧  我会这么说
Okay. Well, it's just...

64
00:02:57,950 --> 00:03:00,460
也只是因为我们有两个单身朋友嘛
we have two single friends.

65
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:02,770
华仔  我才刚认识这女生
Howie, I just met this woman.

66
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:04,770
何不稍微等到我更了解她之后呢
Why don't I wait a little and get to know her?

67
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:07,060
或许我会讨厌她  到时我就会很乐意
Maybe I won't like her, and then I'd be happy

68
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:10,050
让斯图尔特与拉杰毁了她人生
to ruin her life with Stuart or Raj.

69
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:13,490
这样我就满足了
That's all I ask.

70
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,470
你们俩跟谢尔顿同住过很长一段时间
So, you guys lived with Sheldon for a long time...

71
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:20,350
-好长  -太长了
- Long time. - So very long.

72
00:03:20,980 --> 00:03:23,290
对了  再次恭喜你们订婚啊
By the way, congratulations again on your engagement.

73
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:26,520
对啊  你找到了人中之龙啊
Yeah. You got a good one.

74
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:28,730
谢谢  所以有件怪事
Thanks. So, it's strange,

75
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:30,910
谢尔顿昨晚睡觉说梦话了
Sheldon was talking in his sleep last night,

76
00:03:30,910 --> 00:03:33,280
感觉他完全是另一个人
and he seemed like a totally different person.

77
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:35,510
他很放松而且...
He was relaxed and...

78
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:37,720
散漫且平静
loose and calm.

79
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:39,480
谢尔顿是个复杂的男人
Well, Sheldon's a complicated man.

80
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:40,920
他说了"无所"
He said "Whatev."

81
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:44,730
带他去做大脑扫描  可能长脑瘤了
Give him a brain scan-- that might be a tumor.

82
00:03:44,730 --> 00:03:47,590
我觉得计划婚礼对他造成太大压力了
Well, I think the wedding planning is really stressful for him,

83
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,580
从而导致梦呓
and that can trigger sleep talking.

84
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:51,470
或许那是谢尔顿性格中
Well, maybe this is a part of Sheldon's personality

85
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,980
一直被他压抑的一部分
he's been repressing.

86
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,460
毕竟不是正所谓
I mean, I think we dream about things

87
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:56,450
日有所思夜有所梦吗
we wish we could be in real life.

88
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:58,010
是吗  那你都梦些什么了
Really? What do you dream about?

89
00:03:58,010 --> 00:04:01,430
比如当莱纳德的老婆
Oh. Uh... being the wife of Leonard.

90
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,360
基本都是这个啦
Mostly that.

91
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,400
我选择相信你
I choose to believe you.

92
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,880
虽然人类对大脑做过无数研究
Well, as much as we've studied the brain,

93
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,380
但人类对梦与它的作用还是有许多不了解
there's still a lot we don't know about dreams and their function.

94
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:13,550
心理学家们对它的解读也有分歧
You know, even psychologists are divided on it.

95
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:15,890
的确  佛洛依德认为梦与性有关
Mm, it's true-- Freud thought dreams were about sex,

96
00:04:15,890 --> 00:04:22,510
两者曾是同一精神分析学会的核心人物  后者不同意前者看法  因此退出并自成一派

97
00:04:15,890 --> 00:04:17,390
阿德勒认为梦与支配有关
Adler thought they were about dominance...

98
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:22,510
再次强调  我的梦都是与嫁给这位小巨人有关
Then again, mine are just about being married to this little guy.

99
00:04:22,510 --> 00:04:25,790
这次感觉像是在嘲讽我了
Well, now it's just edging into mockery.

100
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:30,310
搬到新的城市真的有些让人害怕
Well, moving to a new city was a little scary,

101
00:04:30,310 --> 00:04:31,510
但这份工作感觉挺不错的
but the job seems great.

102
00:04:31,510 --> 00:04:32,850
大家人都很好
Everyone's really nice.

103
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:34,980
是啊  都超好
Oh, they are. Super nice.

104
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,980
虽然只有一个人晚上带你出来玩
I mean, only one them took you out tonight--

105
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:39,540
但毕竟这也不是什么比赛
but it's not a competition.

106
00:04:39,820 --> 00:04:41,180
再次谢谢你
Thanks again.

107
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:44,240
其实我们可以去更适合孕妇的地方啊
You know, we could have gone somewhere more pregnancy-friendly.

108
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:47,170
没事的  怀孕的其中一个亮点就是
Oh, it's okay. One of the great things about being pregnant

109
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:49,170
可以用酒杯喝蔓越莓汁
is drinking cranberry juice out of a wineglass

110
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:52,120
然后看别人着急的反应
and watching people freak out.

111
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,710
妮妮
Bernie!

112
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,510
我勒个去
Oh, damn.

113
00:04:57,140 --> 00:05:00,290
有缘千里来相会啊
Hey! What are the odds?

114
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:03,770
是啊  真特么"巧"啊
Yeah, seren-frickin'-dipity.

115
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:04,420
你好
Hello.

116
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:06,190
-拉杰什  -斯图尔特
- Rajesh. - Stuart.

117
00:05:06,190 --> 00:05:07,670
我叫如琪
Hi. Ruchi.

118
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:09,190
如琪是我的同事
Ruchi is my coworker.

119
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:13,070
但估计你们在介绍简报里都看过了
But that was probably in your briefing packet.

120
00:05:21,220 --> 00:05:22,650
怎么啦
What's wrong?

121
00:05:22,650 --> 00:05:24,990
我找到了最佳的结婚日了
Well, I found the perfect wedding date.

122
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:27,240
-那太棒啦  -才不呢
- That's terrific! - No, it's not.

123
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:31,250
是1996年5月19日
It was May 19, 1996.

124
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:33,480
我们本来可以有一场完美的婚礼
We would have had a lovely wedding.

125
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,050
我们的蜜月之旅刚好还能对上
And our honeymoon would have coincided

126
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:38,220
该彗星在1995年被发现  于1997年4月1日过近日点

127
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:38,220
海尔-波普彗星的首次出现
with the first appearance of the Hale-Bopp comet.

128
00:05:38,220 --> 00:05:39,780
谢尔顿  你当时才16岁
Sheldon, you were 16.

129
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:43,270
那时我也还在德州  我们那里才没人会管
And in Texas-- no one would have batted an eye.

130
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:44,250
等等  那天也不好
Oh, wait, it's no good.

131
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:47,150
第三任《神秘博士》演员是在那天去世的
That's the day that Jon Pertwee, the third Doctor Who, died.

132
00:05:47,150 --> 00:05:48,430
而且那天已经过了
And it's in the past.

133
00:05:48,430 --> 00:05:51,770
我已经说那天不好了  放下吧
Hey-hey, I said it's no good-- just let it go.

134
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:52,960
谢尔顿
Sheldon...

135
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,760
我很感激你想让婚礼完美的心
I appreciate you trying to make this wedding perfect,

136
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:58,240
但这都快把你搞疯了
but it's making you miserable.

137
00:05:58,240 --> 00:05:59,980
不是  婚礼没有要把我搞疯
No, the wedding isn't making me miserable,

138
00:05:59,980 --> 00:06:01,460
是日子
the calendar is.

139
00:06:01,460 --> 00:06:03,480
为什么名人就不能集中在
Why can't there just be one week each month

140
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:06,510
每个月某周去世呢
for famous people to die?

141
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:10,210
外国的一种迷信  有人认为一个人死去后  会有另外两个与死者有关系的人也跟着过世

142
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:08,480
都已经丧事成三了
Well, they've already arranged to die in threes--

143
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,210
你还想要求人家怎么样啊
what more do you want from them?

144
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:14,170
真是闹心  为什么我就找不出最佳的日子呢
This is so frustrating. Why can't I find a perfect date?

145
00:06:14,170 --> 00:06:16,350
我就找出了与牛仔打招呼的最佳方式啊
I found the perfect way to say hi to cowboys.

146
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:22,380
我只是觉得或许在你内心的深处
I'm just saying maybe there's a part of you deep down that...

147
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:25,110
有一部分的你只想放松下来
just wants to relax a little, you know?

148
00:06:25,110 --> 00:06:26,070
逍遥一点
Kick back.

149
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:28,520
比如说出"无所..."
Say, "Whatev."

150
00:06:29,170 --> 00:06:31,350
无所...吗
Whatev?

151
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:34,270
抱歉  你真的不把那词说完吗
I'm sorry, you're really not gonna finish that word?

152
00:06:34,270 --> 00:06:35,730
我只是举个例子嘛
I-I'm just trying to make a point...

153
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:38,220
说完它  艾米
Finish the word, Amy.

154
00:06:38,220 --> 00:06:40,340
行  谓
Fine. Er.

155
00:06:40,340 --> 00:06:41,850
谓  谓  谓
Er, er, er.

156
00:06:41,850 --> 00:06:42,950
谢谢
Thank you.

157
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:46,060
但你现在欠我三次"无所"了
Only now you owe me three more whatevs.

158
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:50,450
原来你是印度特里凡得琅出生的啊
Oh, you were born in Trivandrum.

159
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:53,010
你去过那里的百马宫了吗
Have you ever been to the Kuthira Malika Palace?

160
00:06:53,010 --> 00:06:54,380
没  没去过呢
No, I haven't.

161
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:57,640
我也是呢  真是太有缘了
Me, either. What a small world.

162
00:06:58,090 --> 00:06:59,760
我也没去过那里
I've also never been there.

163
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:01,390
我没去过的地方太多了
I've never been lots of places.

164
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:03,640
来啊  考我看看
Go on, quiz me.

165
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,180
对不起  我们这么聊印度的事太无礼了
I'm sorry, we're being rude talking about India.

166
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,720
是啊  如果你跟伯纳黛特
Oh, yeah, you know, if you and Bernadette

167
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:10,060
想聊美国的事  我们没意见的
want to talk about America, that's cool with us.

168
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,920
我来帮你们起个头吧
Here, let me get you started.

169
00:07:11,920 --> 00:07:14,920
汉堡包  对吧
Hamburgers. Am I right?

170
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,910
你们都做什么工作
So, what do you guys do?

171
00:07:17,910 --> 00:07:20,390
我是个天体物理学家
Well, I am an astrophysicist,

172
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:23,720
如果你哪天晚上出去看仰望星空
so if you ever go out at night and look up at the stars,

173
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:25,850
也能算是看入我的办公室呢
that's kind of my office.

174
00:07:25,850 --> 00:07:29,320
他卖漫画书给孩子
He sells comic books to children.

175
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:30,550
其实呢
Actually,

176
00:07:30,550 --> 00:07:32,320
我是自己开的店
I own my own store.

177
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,650
如果你有兴趣来看看
Uh, I-if you'd like to check it out sometime,

178
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:35,910
我最近在做个促销活动
I'm running a new promotion--

179
00:07:35,910 --> 00:07:40,140
买任何东西  就请你吃价钱合理的晚餐一次
buy anything, get taken out for a reasonably priced dinner.

